# Security headers for the admin SPA, applied by Cloudflare Pages to every response.
# CSP allows only what this app actually loads: same-origin scripts/styles/API calls. Unlike
# apps/client, admin never renders TMDb poster images, so img-src stays same-origin. style-src needs
# 'unsafe-inline' because several components set inline `style={{...}}` (React's normal way of
# setting dynamic CSS, e.g. StatsOverview, ContentModerationContent); nothing here needs
# 'unsafe-inline'/'unsafe-eval' on script-src.
#
# connect-src is 'self' because the supported deploy topology is same-origin (apps/admin and
# services/api sharing a registrable domain, or a Pages proxy) -- see docs/runbook.md's "Cross-site
# cookies" section. If VITE_API_URL ever points at a different origin, connect-src needs that origin
# added too, or API calls will be blocked by this policy before they even reach the cookie problem.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
